There is a new class of the O11 kind that no SPEC text names. A sub-visible move of the Grip parts alone moves twins about the grip, and with them G (O11 names its classes; §5.6's 'grip nudges' row covers only EdgeLength). On every 3rd plausible design (11,130), with every Grip part moved 1e-9:
- along Z, G moves on 1,274, by up to 0.0471, 8 a played tier;
- along X, G moves on 858, 1 a tier;
- 1,496 move on one axis or the other (13.4 %).

On every 9th design (3,710), f7ac37d moves Z 0 and X 5 (up to 0.0037, no tier). The tree, on the same 3,710, moves Z 432 (2 tiers) and X 285 (1). P5 with its grip 1e-9 along +X: Hammering 0.2167 Hard → 0.1902 Normal (f7ac37d 0.2167). The hidden-part chain above is the same mechanism with a hidden part doing the choosing.

I tried 31 mutants of the six guards. The suite catches 14:
- mF_p6Every, mG_expEvery, mR_placeFloor, mS_signFirst, mT_vSignFirst;
- mK_asymY, mM_rowsD0, mN_v3gjk;
- mJ_zRaw, mJv_zRaw, mL_slot;
- mO_tol9, mV_plus (box test at +OVERLAP_TOL), mP_reach6.

17 change behaviour and pass every non-timing test:
- mA_notOdd (place rounds half up on both sides);
- mB_centre (grip point from part centres);
- mE_ownEvery (ownership ranked from every Grip part);
- mK_asymX and mK_asymZ (candidate box back at reach on X or Z);
- mU_flat12 and mX_ceil12 (CELL_EPS 1e-12);
- mV_ovHalf (box test at −OVERLAP_TOL/2);
- mW_xgrid8 and mW_xgrid10 (X_GRID 1e8 and 1e10);
- mY_rankQ6 and mZ_rankQ12 (RANK_Q 1e-6 and 1e-12);
- mN_v3broad (V3's broad phase at CONTACT_TOL);
- mM_rowsM0 (contact rows' box margin max(CONTACT_TOL, 2·lim));
- mI_unweighted (unweighted grip point);
- mO_tol6 (OVERLAP_TOL 1e-6);
- mQ_mirror4 (MIRROR_GUARD 1e-4).

Correction to my earlier progress line: mM_rowsM0 is not equivalent. Ball samples have no patch (2·lim = 2e-7; 1.17 M weighted samples on 8,019 designs fall below the reach). On F2 with a Ball pommel d 0.24 exactly 0.01 under its grip, the mutant's Joints read 4.6332 → 4.656 at 6 of 40 Y moves; the tree reads 4.6332 at all of them.
